						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p>His family calls him Leroy, his friends call him Elroy (L. Roy), his acquaintances call him Lee, nobody calls him Roy, and his enemies call him Carl.</p> <p>Dr. Carlson is not, nor has he ever been, affiliated with the Shark Punching Center in any way, shape, or form. He will continue saying it until you believe him. No one has ever once seen him punching a shark, and even if they did what of it? Lots of people hate sharks! They're dangerous and scary! Stop looking at him like that! He loves it here at the SPC!</p> <p>No, please, he meant to say SCP, he swears! It's an easy mistake to make! Don't&#8230;</p> <p><em>Dr. Carlson is currently unavailable. Please leave a message after the cognitohazard.</em></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Things Dr. Carlson has not punched,</strong> and wouldn't punch even if they were sharks:</p> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4225">SCP-4225</a> - Sammy the Superfluous Serpent, by Sr. Supertainment. First (and so far only) installment in a series of Amazing Alliterative Animals, a less successful sequel series to Wondertainment's award-winning Little Misters line of toys.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4314">SCP-4314</a> - An Irrational Number. A pattern screamer hidden in the digits of pi, very poorly executed because I don't understand math very well. Will rewrite this sonuva eventually, possibly after a deletion.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4820">SCP-4820</a> - The Custom of the Sea. My most popular article, because people just can't get enough autocannibalism. Really sucked at the beginning because of unnecessary Sarkic bullshit, but it's much better now. Probably should have let it get deleted and repost to shed the downvotes from the bad versions, but it's too late now.</li> </ul> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p><strong>Stories that are not about Dr. Carlson punching sharks:</strong></p> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/halloween-on-17