Other things people have accused him of being involved with:</strong></p> <ul> <li>I added an iron maiden that plays &quot;Iron Maiden&quot;, from Iron Maiden's album <em>Iron Maiden</em>, to one of the anomalous object logs. Not sure if it's still there, can't be bothered to check.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/interviews-with-prospective-groups-of-interest">Interviews with Prospective Groups of Interest</a>. I blame Clef. I once had an entry here for the RPC too, but was informed that that was both against the author's wishes and in extremely bad taste.</li> </ul> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p><strong>Dr. Carlson's greatest failures.</strong> Their untimely deaths were not due to being punched.</p> <ul> <li>SCP-5081 - PACt-MAN. An Atari Arcadia clone of Pac-Man with a demon and some souls trapped inside it. You can soak quarters in the blood of murder victims and trade their souls to the demon in exchange for wishes. Didn't turn out well on the site for reasons I can't even remember, but I haven't given up on it.</li> <li>SCP-5930-EX - Pablo Neruda's (formerly) toxic mongoose. Pablo Neruda's pet mongoose, who'd been implanted with a poison capsule in a failed attempt to assassinate him. The Foundation thought the mongoose was anomalously sweating poison, and by the time they figured out what was actually going on it was no longer plausible to give him his pet back, so they kept it and made it the Site pet. This was my entry in the Exquisite Corpse contest, so I claim no more than 50% of the blame for its failure. My part was pretty bad, though.</li> <li>I once asked Clef if he liked my idea for an <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-166">SCP-166</a> rewrite, but he never responded, probably because I'm too new to be restoring the works of the masters. The one that did happen was better than mine anyway, though.</li> </ul> </blockquote> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kothardarastrix" ><img class="small